  "howToColoring": "Pick a colour and tap an area to fill it. On Advanced you paint by numbers: each number belongs to one colour. A hint fills one area for you.",
  "howToPixelArt": "Every number stands for a colour. Pick a colour below, then tap or swipe over the matching squares until the picture is done.",
  "howToWordGuess": "Guess the word in six tries. Green: right letter, right spot. Yellow: in the word, wrong spot. Grey: not in the word.",
  "howToAnagram": "The letters are jumbled. Tap them in the right order to build the word. Tap a placed letter to take it back from there.",
  "howToWordSearch": "Find every word in the grid. Drag from the first to the last letter – across, down or diagonally.",
  "howToQuoteQuiz": "Read the quote and tap the person who said it. The questions come from the “Zitat des Tages” app.",
  "howToTrueFalse": "Is the statement right? Tap “True” or “False”. On Advanced you get ten seconds per statement.",
  "howToSudoku": "Fill the grid so every number appears exactly once in each row, column and box. Tap a cell, then a number. Use “Notes” to keep track of candidates.",
  "howToNonogram": "The numbers on the edge tell you how many cells in a row are filled. Fill the right cells to reveal a picture. Mark sure gaps with the cross.",
  "howToLightsOut": "A tap toggles a light and its neighbours. Switch every light off.",
  "howToHanoi": "Move the whole tower to the right peg. Tap a peg to lift its top disc, then tap the target. Never put a bigger disc on a smaller one.",
  "howToMaze": "Guide the dot to the goal. Swipe in a direction or use the arrows.",
  "howToStacking": "The block swings back and forth. Tap to drop it. Whatever overhangs falls off. Build the tower up to the target height.",
  "howToMinesweeper": "Uncover every cell without a mine. A number tells how many mines touch that cell. Use the flag to mark suspects. Your first tap is always safe.",
  "howTo2048": "Swipe to slide all tiles. Equal numbers merge. Reach the target number.",
  "howToNumberPyramid": "Each brick is the sum of the two bricks below it. Fill the empty bricks, then check.",
  "howToMemory": "Turn over two cards at a time. Find all pairs with as few misses as possible.",
  "howToSimon": "Watch the colour sequence, then tap it back. Each round adds one colour.",
  "howToSlidePuzzle": "Slide tiles into the gap until the picture is whole again. Tap a tile next to the gap.",
  "howToBreathing": "Breathe with the circle: in as it grows, hold briefly, out as it shrinks. Nothing to win, just calm.",
